  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="d9cc4b8a-6f38-5233-b774-544f47d8378f" activityNameId="96fd257a-ce45-5a13-84ed-873b874250d2" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Polystyrene, extruded (XPS) CO2 blown, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Polystyrene, extruded (XPS) CO2 blown, at plant
This dataset can be used in the construction building sector. The cutting of the extruded polystyrene blocks is not included in the process. Blowing agent is CO2  (50.7% w/w). Co-blowing agent ist aceton (49.3% w/w). Process emissions are 25% (w/w) for aceton.;
Synonyms: XPS; 
UUID: 46b4182a-4f28-3329-bb90-8e62e9410b30
The dataset describes the production of extruded polystyrene. Included processes are the melting of polystyrene pearls in the extruder, the discharge through a slot die, as well as the cooling with water.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Extrusion process of expandable polystyrene including discharge via slot die. CO2 as blowing agents, aceton as Co-blowing agent.
Time period: Technology in 1994 was still using CFC or HCFC as blowing agent. In 2005, already more than 50% of companies in Europe are using CO2 as blowing agent. Though mainly in the USA, HFC-134a and HFC-152a as a blowing agent are still common.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature, database 
Extrapolations: see Geography
Uncertainty adjustments: The assumption that Germany is representative for Central Europe is considered in the uncertainties.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_46b4182a-4f28-3329-bb90-8e62e9410b30.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
